{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And any person who eats a carcass or a torn animal.</b> After writing the matter of the prohibition of blood, which draws association with demons, He spoke of one who eats a carcass or a torn animal — which prepares him for an unclean spirit to rest upon him, as they said in Sanhedrin, chapter Four Deaths: וְדוֹרֵשׁ אֶל הַמֵּתִים (Deuteronomy 18:11) — 'this is one who starves himself and goes to sleep in a graveyard so that an unclean spirit may rest upon him.'"], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:42.831129188Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}